package landings

import (
	"github.com/gofiber/fiber/v2"
	"journal/internal/web"
)

templ AboutPage(c *fiber.Ctx) {
	@web.Base(c, &web.Head{Title: "About"}) {
		<section class="landing" id="about-page">
			<h2>About This Journal</h2>
			<p>I built this for myself.</p>
			<p>I was going through a hard time and started therapy, and kept running into a problem -- by the time I sat down with my therapist, I wasn't in the same headspace I'd been in when things were difficult. I figured journaling might help me capture things at the time of them happening. Pen and paper didn't stick, and the digital journals I looked at either chained me to my phone or felt like platforms doing something with my data I didn't fully agree with. So I built my own.</p>
			<p>I still think there's something to writing by hand that this doesn't fully replicate. But this is the version I actually kept using.</p>
			<h3>What it does</h3>
			<p>It's a place to put thoughts honestly, because nothing here is analyzing what you write and there's no reason to hold back. Something happens when you put a feeling into words that doesn't happen when you just carry it around. It's not immediately gone, but you've kind of dealt with it.</p>
			<p>Alongside the writing, you can log a quick rating, jot down small actions that come out of what you wrote, and note things worth being grateful for. Over time those pieces add up to patterns you might not have noticed otherwise.</p>
			<h3>What it isn't</h3>
			<p>This isn't a therapy tool. It won't analyze your writing, tell you how you should feel, or remind you that you missed a day. No streaks, no gamification, no AI reading your entries. The point is to process and mostly leave it.</p>
			<h3>Privacy, actually</h3>
			<p>All entries, actions, and thankfuls are encrypted. No ads, no tracking, no data selling. There's a blur mode if you're somewhere public. None of that is a feature, it's just how a journal should work.</p>
			<h3>One person, one project</h3>
			<p>This is built and maintained by one person who uses it himself. If you have thoughts, ideas, feature requests, or run into something broken, there's a <a href="/feedback">feedback form</a> and someone actually reads it.</p>
			<p>The optional paid features exist mostly to support the project. The core journal is fully functional without them, and that's intentional -- this isn't trying to lock anyone out of anything useful. No subscriptions, ever.</p>
			<p>If you find the journal useful and just want to say thanks, there's a <a href="https://buymeacoffee.com/drkgrntt2" target="_blank">link for that too</a>.</p>
		</section>
	}
}
